Description: UAC hash_executables - a hash of every executable file, for checking against a hash set
Category: Integrity
Author: ArtefactForge
Version: '1.0'
ExportFormat: csv
OutputName: LinuxExecutableHashes
# UAC's hash_executables lists a hash of every executable file on the system, one list per
# algorithm (hash_executables.md5, .sha1, .sha256). They are merged into one row per file, ready to
# check against a known-good or known-bad hash set. Executables in temporary or shared-memory
# folders, or in hidden folders, are marked in the Review column.
#
# Reads %root%\_UAC\hash_executables, where a UAC collection's lists land on extraction.
Requires:
  - '%root%/_UAC/hash_executables'
Platform: linux
Priority: 46
IoWeight: light
Processors:
  -
    Executable: builtin:LinuxExecutableHashes
    CommandLine: --root "%root%" --out "%destinationDirectory%"
    ExportFormat: csv
